.TH TULPAR-ROLLBACK 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.3.1" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-rollback, tulpar-undo \- undo the most recent package operation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar rollback
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar undo
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar b
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar \-b
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects the database audit journal to find the most recent successful
transaction batch and inverts its operations:
packages installed during that operation are removed, and packages
removed during that operation are re-installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Operate against the database of an alternate root.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes and skip confirmation prompts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-history (1),
.BR tulpar-install (1),
.BR tulpar-remove (1)
